    "Generic click model rho(a,k): click probability depends on the whole recommendation and the position; assumed to satisfy strict weak order on items (3.1), optimality of order-compatible recommendations (3.2) and order identifiability via expected click differences (3.3)",
    "Learner knows number of items L and number of positions K",
    "Reward is the number of clicks (sum over positions)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "An instance of our OLR problem is a tuple (L, K, ρ), where L is the number of available items, K ⩽ L is the number of positions to display the items, and ρ is a function from P_K^L × [K] to (0, 1] such that for any recommendation a and position k, ρ(a, k) is the probability for a user to click on the item displayed at position k when recommending a. A recommendation algorithm is only aware of L and K and has to deliver T consecutive recommendations."
